robco-term (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * On macOS the settings window is reached the way a Mac reaches things:
    Ctrl+click as the right-click, and a Settings item on Cmd+, in the
    application menu the platform draws.
  * Cmd holds the unbroken copy of a wrapped selection on macOS, Ctrl
    being the secondary click there; Ctrl still holds it elsewhere.
  * Cmd+Q closes the terminal through its own shutdown, so the
    single-instance socket and lock are cleared rather than left behind.

